      ],
      "source": "https://ocmohistory.wordpress.com/2025/03/23/oregon-county-history-thomasville-community/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When Oregon County formed in 1841, Thomasville became its first county seat, covering parts of modern Howell, Shannon, and Carter Counties.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomasville%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office operated in Thomasville from 1846 until 1979, marking over a century of mail service.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomasville%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s public library, part of the Oregon County library system, serves residents and preserves local history.",
